===============================================================================
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
===============================================================================

Bloomery builds on the following works. Their licenses are compatible with the
AGPL, and their terms continue to apply to their own code. Where bloomery
includes or adapts their source directly, that is noted.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
nanochat — https://github.com/karpathy/nanochat
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Andrej Karpathy

An influence, not a dependency. Bloomery's "depth dial" — deriving width, head
count, MLP size and learning rate from a single layer count — is borrowed in
spirit from nanochat. No nanochat source is included or adapted; bloomery builds
on the Llama implementation in `transformers` instead. Credited because the idea
is worth crediting.

